      "text": "This problem involves a series of sizes that bounces up from bottom height to the top and then falls again. It can be seen that the highest one is above the sum of the series, i.e., when subtracting the lowest sum from the highest sum, another sum occurs, which is the low low. So I divide $243$ by $30$ and get the answer.\n\nI use inverse proportion.\n$$243\\times \\frac{30}{243}b=121$$\nwhere $b$ is the lowest sum, which comes from formula Tn-A1=Num/2 and $$b=2+(1+n)\\times \\frac{22}{30}$$ $$b=\\boxed{36}$$",
